+If expansion reaches thousands, simplify repeated microstructure before execution, retaining each
+inventory object and meaningful parts. Represent unresolved surface detail using shared materials
+and restrained procedural shading. Avoid per-element decoration below image resolution.
+Use short adaptively spaced tube paths with points concentrated at bends. Avoid many nearly
+identical Boolean slices for one hollow form; use a small number of suitable solids and cutters
+while preserving the visible opening. Prefer boxes or scaled balls when their silhouettes suffice.
+Reserve fillet_box for parts whose rounded edges matter. Avoid a separate random material for
